{"title":"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Geometric)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Geometric)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2B\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2B</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Using_Answer_Choice_+_Calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Using Answer Choice + Calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Lagrange_Multipliers)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Lagrange Multipliers)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(polar_coordinates)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (polar coordinates)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Alcumus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Alcumus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/e/a6e244a99a7f4091a8cef03c416efd9725b4f27d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = 14x + 6y + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />, what is the largest possible value that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc716a6b531f16838d00e426373f054e3929383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> can have? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/3/3f3fdeeab533b180f28633523cb1309aa362b5c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 72\\qquad\\text{(B)}\\ 73\\qquad\\text{(C)}\\ 74\\qquad\\text{(D)}\\ 75\\qquad\\text{(E)}\\ 76$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Complete the square to get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/a/a9a574a1a47876253cf3169f35c9e9aeb327e312.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-7)^2 + (y-3)^2 = 64.\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"20\" />\nApplying Cauchy-Schwarz directly,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/756b22487ee619c4b3f84ee1e5ce1c78e931dfaa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[64\\cdot25=(3^2+4^2)((x-7)^2 + (y-3)^2) \\ge (3(x-7)+4(y-3))^2.\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b14accbcab552b6c355b0d445864adcdb3f5793.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[40 \\ge 3x+4y-33\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/0280b4acb9baa3f23e73a5c6d05fc7e46c177db3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3x+4y \\le 73.\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" />\nThus our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a558b37c441e1b7ac7c5ff6a848f199ac53ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Geometric.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Geometric)\">Solution 2 (Geometric)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Geometric)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first equation is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a>, so we find its center and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radius</a> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Completing_the_square\" title=\"Completing the square\">completing the square</a>: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31ad0cf24c7522cbb4714af2e04f6a7e7c55f32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 14x + y^2 - 6y = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/7/797e383ff9731b6e5ea92ffae3a41149cea145a7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x-7)^2 + (y-3)^2 = (x^2- 14x + 49) + (y^2 - 6y + 9) = 6 + 49 + 9 = 64.\\]\" width=\"489\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>So we have a circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c74fb9c2531de69ae495a9220765cd08a070c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and we want to find the max of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc716a6b531f16838d00e426373f054e3929383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>The set of lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0ed8cccd915c2d111e839bef11dfaab7839bf58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y = A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" /> are all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallel\" title=\"Parallel\">parallel</a>, with slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/dee6596f6d34c586070c53b458cf129f8c513e05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" />.  Increasing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> shifts the lines up and/or to the right.\n</p><p>We want to shift this line up high enough that it's <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tangent_(geometry)\" title=\"Tangent (geometry)\">tangent</a> to the circle, but not so high that it misses the circle altogether.  This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/d/0ed8cccd915c2d111e839bef11dfaab7839bf58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y = A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" /> will be tangent to the circle.\n</p><p>Imagine that this line hits the circle at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />.  The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Slope\" title=\"Slope\">slope</a> of the radius connecting the center of the circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c74fb9c2531de69ae495a9220765cd08a070c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, to tangent point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b33bd495b7492f95385da7afb197cd34638cdfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />, since the radius is perpendicular to the tangent line.\n</p><p>So we have a point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c74fb9c2531de69ae495a9220765cd08a070c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and a slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b33bd495b7492f95385da7afb197cd34638cdfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> that represents the slope of the radius to the tangent point.  Let's start at the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c74fb9c2531de69ae495a9220765cd08a070c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />.  If we go <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8dfc0a791aaa72566aa16f59251abceb117de6ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> units up and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/6/ce6582d1a31d1fd6bdab19f0d332c8d93adb9c66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> units right from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c74fb9c2531de69ae495a9220765cd08a070c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, we would arrive at a point that's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/c/58cbd31c5e7955bcfbc1e50dd82bf1d54160bbba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5k$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> units away.  But in reality we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a919ac110a39e2c1513cc45ca65554bf088aaa98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5k = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> to reach the tangent point, since the radius of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42cf7617f459d0d76acb475d00772fc9d5dd45e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\frac{8}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />, and we want to travel <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/1/7c1efaa927e8a3b7fd2de6fdb3da1ca76f4bd402.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\cdot \\frac{8}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"33\" height=\"37\" /> up and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12c1f2e612e0e458f3e40c14e6eee2fb4a4d9022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot \\frac{8}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"33\" height=\"37\" /> over from the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c74fb9c2531de69ae495a9220765cd08a070c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> to reach our maximum.  This means the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc716a6b531f16838d00e426373f054e3929383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> occurs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/6015f7b477f6a0be24eda7b5670e3c3e75632cce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(7 +3\\cdot \\frac{8}{5}, 3 + 4\\cdot \\frac{8}{5}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"164\" height=\"43\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fb002695d17f2cd56fa72c10969c117a6b48197.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{59}{5}, \\frac{47}{5}\\right).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"85\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Plug in those values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and you get the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/d/5ad2263f2dca4fc86b29774b09a944e02f65336b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y = 3\\cdot\\frac{59}{5} + 4\\cdot\\frac{47}{5} = \\boxed{73}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"249\" height=\"37\" />, which is option <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a558b37c441e1b7ac7c5ff6a848f199ac53ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2B\">Solution 2B</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2B\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the tangent point be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and the tangent line's x-intercept be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Consider the horizontal line starting from center of circle (O) meeting the tangent line at K. Now triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/7691173d0be863ccf05b2d6aa73ca6f12d454db9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OPK$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" /> is 3-4-5, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bca4ffae4bf9622645452727836e3e477d015614.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP=8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/2/3b2ab47f6b0aaea794bd3735cd4700bc469a2082.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OK = \\frac{5}{3}*8 = \\frac{40}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"139\" height=\"37\" />. Note that the horizontal distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the origin is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the horizontal distance from K to Q is 4, (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b33bd495b7492f95385da7afb197cd34638cdfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> of its y coordinate), so the x-intercept is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/8/af8b34e69a3e2d3fb009486ad9c5baf8420407d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7+4+OK = 73/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"20\" />. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/3/913e3f046a640de9f4fa5e37bdd5a369f44ca62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x+4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> is 73 at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Note that this value is constant on the tangent line, so there is no need to calculate the coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a558b37c441e1b7ac7c5ff6a848f199ac53ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/7/cf7d4742a8c00053b602a87dd7defab18d3224eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 3x + 4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/b/2dbe75e1c3f20462c04fd1fd7e9a1d93d93c93b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = (z - 3x)/4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />. Substituting into the given equation, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/5878f2d99264578dd397046ad06fd6eb2a497b88.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 + \\left( \\frac{z - 3x}{4} \\right)^2 = 14x + 6 \\cdot \\frac{z - 3x}{4} + 6,\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"46\" />\nwhich simplifies to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/330426b30e3e4bc88c45ac43be94cbb48d4642e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[25x^2 - (6z + 152)x + (z^2 - 24z - 96) = 0.\\]\" width=\"330\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>This quadratic equation has real roots in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> if and only if its discriminant is nonnegative, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e0dee43a784de3fb8bab5039aca4aa6672b625b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(6z + 152)^2 - 4 \\cdot 25 \\cdot (z^2 - 24z - 96) \\ge 0,\\]\" width=\"322\" height=\"19\" />\nwhich simplifies to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/a/09ae49375323976fb8345e09b7f2c70e5f347ca3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-64z^2 + 4224z + 32704 \\ge 0,\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />\nwhich can be factored as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ed30b6c34d157c44122de89dae78ddc870c766.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-64(z + 7)(z - 73) \\ge 0.\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" />\nThe largest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies this inequality is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a0c1085eb3ba5eb6376bc00e7ea24690c680775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{73}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a558b37c441e1b7ac7c5ff6a848f199ac53ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Using_Answer_Choice_.2B_Calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Using_Answer_Choice_+_Calculus)\">Solution 4 (Using Answer Choice + Calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Using Answer Choice + Calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Implicitly differentiating the given equation with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> yields:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8eb5911ee47d8b1c31dcf27b3b2b39490142a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 2y\\frac{dy}{dx} = 14 + 6\\frac{dy}{dx}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"184\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Now solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/916bee646822bba385ea2564c810ecd5fa0ac0b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{dy}{dx}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"22\" height=\"37\" /> to obtain:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b69d0ed5dcb0ddb71e03f40d3b2b4ab186a84a51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{dy}{dx} = -\\frac{x - 7}{y - 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"106\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Set the equation equal to zero to find the maximum occurs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d1e7375e601943b3bb958a24e41da8920d601a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Plug this back into the equation that we are trying to maximize and see that we are left with: \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/5760442d7777470c7b3f16d6081a67d1414a40c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21 + 4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The only answer choice that can be obtained from this equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/deb1691036fd48016309f70de017b0d7f0a48724.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bf{73}$\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Note: In the correct solution, y is not an integer, but here y is assumed to be an integer -inaccessibles\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Lagrange_Multipliers.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Lagrange_Multipliers)\">Solution 5 (Lagrange Multipliers)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Lagrange Multipliers)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we move all the non-constant terms of the constraint to one side and assign it to the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e13f2c74e18e89468e2e32c39dd142efaefad98e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c18cc5df4b45dcd9738285389bc809a94c18d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(x,y)=x^2+y^2-14x-6y.\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"20\" />\nSince we are trying to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/e/5de2e9c84808d2371d1e56d184d2bf4bec394afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x,y)=3x+4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"18\" />, we need to solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in the system\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd77e1ea98975a2d0a4781d2cb12fdce1337eb21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{cases}x^2+y^2-14x-6y=6,\\\\\\nabla g(x,y)=\\lambda\\nabla f(x,y).\\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"53\" />\nWe have that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/297383126a898d66a87a7b7138af056e97bbb995.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\nabla f(x,y)&amp;=\\begin{pmatrix}\\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial x}3x+4y\\\\\\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial y}3x+4y\\end{pmatrix}\\\\&amp;=\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\4\\end{pmatrix},\\end{align*}\" width=\"203\" height=\"128\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2cdc22fe37385e725df580c6272a38f2f839581.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\nabla g(x,y)&amp;=\\begin{pmatrix}\\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial x}x^2+y^2-14x-6y\\\\\\dfrac{\\partial}{\\partial y}x^2+y^2-14x-6y\\end{pmatrix}\\\\&amp;=\\begin{pmatrix}2x-14\\\\2y-6\\end{pmatrix}\\end{align*}.\" width=\"382\" height=\"148\" />\nTo solve the original system, we can solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> using our equations from the gradients, then substitute them into the first equation. We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8363be4b91b9c61fec4867af05a0b788c36f335d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{3}{2}\\lambda+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cf765e33165cea6b36ef8028bebd988862d9664.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2\\lambda+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />. Substituting into the first equation, we have that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3c2cf08be288a71cbea91ce043f123b4c2dc51a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\lambda+7\\right)^2+(2\\lambda+3)^2-14\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\lambda+7\\right)-6(2\\lambda+3)&amp;=6\\\\\\frac{25}{4}\\lambda^2&amp;=64\\\\\\lambda&amp;=\\pm\\frac{16}{5}\\end{align*}\" width=\"460\" height=\"133\" />\nUsing the solutions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> that we found earlier, we have that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2d2e77995c2c0b2ebef22fd566726c95cdc6e20.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3x+4y=\\frac{25}{2}\\lambda+33.\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"38\" />\nBecause we are trying to maximize this function, we will use the positive solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4588fd900d02afcbd260bc07f54cce49a7dc4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda$\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" />. Therefore, after substituting, we have that the largest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e13f2c74e18e89468e2e32c39dd142efaefad98e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/303e57601b4ab713acf61b09dce212fdf90631a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x,y)=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc20f060e74da03d9f6eb245b1779dfc1fbc75e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }73}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~qianqian07\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28polar_coordinates.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(polar_coordinates)\">Solution 6 (polar coordinates)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (polar coordinates)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Completing the square gives the equation of a circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/6/9e6f6c0cd6ebbc8a293ec15978e613e22ca621ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-7)^2+(y-3)^2=64.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"193\" height=\"19\" /> Seeing that we would like to maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a0bf6bfdef1cd4bdbaed81cc7e3083a90300d29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x+4y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> we parameterize the circle using polar coordinates:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5fb684c1c27ccc571a1e02914be30f5c687ee66.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x&amp;=7+8\\cos\\theta&amp;y&amp;=3+8\\sin\\theta. \\end{align*}\" width=\"312\" height=\"16\" />\nThen, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfee669b8add852e10a903284c1baea16c96b4b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x+4y=3(7+8\\cos\\theta)+4(3+8\\sin\\theta)=33+24\\cos\\theta+32\\sin\\theta.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"518\" height=\"20\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/1437fac67fac696b9327447c56f063168aab677a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\cos\\theta+b\\sin\\theta\\le\\sqrt{a^2+b^2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"217\" height=\"22\" /> the desired answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2f2f2e4a84dbea52500724064c412fdd627d71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33+\\sqrt{24^2+32^2}=33+40=\\boxed{73}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"272\" height=\"25\" />\n- Ultroid999OCPN\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Alcumus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Alcumus)\">Solution 6 (Alcumus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Alcumus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/e/a6e244a99a7f4091a8cef03c416efd9725b4f27d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = 14x + 6y + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" /> can be written <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db676e1badaf8cee6a10de2ac290d2cab0d0fabc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-7)^2 + (y-3)^2 = 8^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"21\" />, which defines a circle of radius 8 centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c74fb9c2531de69ae495a9220765cd08a070c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc716a6b531f16838d00e426373f054e3929383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> on the circle, then the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/6/a2669798d6acf99c793a1411c4814083521a226a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> must intersect the circle in at least one point. The largest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> occurs when the line is tangent to the circle, and is therefore perpendicular to the radius at the point of tangency. Because the slope of the tangent line is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1ea4d8f0bcd1de0d9a921bbbde93176f584c38df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3/4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" /> the slope of the radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79eb8e19631d2e3949d5b0dedf357abbb6eb2bcf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />. It follows that the point on the circle that yields the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc716a6b531f16838d00e426373f054e3929383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> is one of the two points of tangency, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/b/95bac54a66ce77947189f5f67452a6f083601c0a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 7 + \\frac{3 \\cdot 8}{5} = \\frac{59}{5}, \\qquad y = 3 +\\frac{4 \\cdot 8}{5} = \\frac{47}{5},\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/b/3eb65f352ab3605cd45e60a6a1df8aef193b96e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 7 - \\frac{3 \\cdot 8}{5} = \\frac{11}{5}, \\qquad y = 3 \\frac{4 \\cdot 8}{5} = - \\frac{17}{5}.\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><br />\n[asy]\nimport olympiad; import geometry; size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));\ndraw((0,15)--origin--(15,0));\ndot(\"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c74fb9c2531de69ae495a9220765cd08a070c92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />\",(7,3),S);\ndraw(Circle((7,3),8));\nline a = line((0,9),(12,0));\nline b = line((0,12),(16,0));\nline c = line((0,18.3),(18.3*4/3,0));\ndraw(a^^b^^c);\n[/asy]\n</p><p>The first point of tangency gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/3/20383f24e3226636ab46359729ef27edc8bfdd4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 4y = 3 \\cdot \\frac{59}{5} + 4 \\cdot \\frac{47}{5} =\\frac{177}{5}+\\frac{188}{5}= 73,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"354\" height=\"38\" /> and the second one gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/6200a45e0f22fa18c91afcba11d7a0358418da12.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\, 3x + 4y = \\frac{33}{5}-\\frac{68}{5} = -7.\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"37\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a0c1085eb3ba5eb6376bc00e7ea24690c680775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{73}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> is the desired maximum, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea223a5d7cfe61a2a37366de9f2a31d6b4d9b9db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-7$\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> is the minimum.\n</p><p>[b]Please resubmit without unrendered LaTeX or asymptote. ~NathanBikeSki[/b]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME\" title=\"1996 AHSME\">1996 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1996 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1996\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1996 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1996 AHS